%T Transition Phenomena in Cellular Automata Rule Space
%A W. Li
%A N. H. Packard
%A C. G. Langton
%B Cellular Automata Theory and Experiment
%E H. Gutowitz
%I MIT Press
%D 1991
%X
Argue that bay varying lambda one can get phase transition
(first and second order) from ``simpl\('e' periodic rule to chaotic rules
and that ``complex'' rule lies at the phase transition border.
type of rule obtained from statistical measures.
appendix explain the computation methods for some statictical quantities:
spreading rate of difference patterns, entropy and mutual information
and for the spreading rate of difference pattern by mean-field theory
also propose some refinement to the wolfram classification
(mainly about shifting configuration space)

%T Is There a Sharp Phase Transition for Deterministic Cellular Automata?
%A W. K. Wootters
%A C. G. Langton
%B Cellular Automata Theory and Experiment
%E H. Gutowitz
%I MIT Press
%D 1991
%X
Try to find a ``sharp phase transition'' in the limit large rules tables
(mainly by augmenting the number of symbols).
use mean field theory to predict statistical properties (mainly entropy)
using lambda as parameter.

